Monitoring

Monitoring is tracking the health , performance and activity of a system
so problem can be detected then take action ideally before they cause damage.

1.Infrastructure monitoring = Is the server alive ? are resources sufficient
2.Application monitoring = Is app working correctly ? are there errors
3.Log monitoring = What even happened on the system/app
4.Security monitoring = Was there unauthorized/suspicious activity.

Monitoring Tool Stack.
1.Cloud Native Tool (AWS native : CloudWatch ,CloudTrail)
2.Third party Tool/Open source (Prometheus , Grafana ,Datadog , new Relic)

Concept Wise Monitoring.
1.Push Based : The server send its own data to the monitoring system.
2.Pull Based : The monitoring system goes to the server to fetch data .(scrap it)
3.Real-time and batch/schedule/periodic monitoring.
4.Black-box and white-box monitoring
Black-box : Testing from outside , without looking internals. (Uptime , ping , Http-check)
White-box : Looking at system internal metrics and logs . (CPU/Memory , application internal logs)
5.Sythetic Monitoring : Bots system check
6.Real User monitoring (RUM) : Real human user check everything's and collect data.


